  "interpretation": [
    "Native physics executes on CPU and returns CUDA tensors; Warp physics executes on CUDA. These are explicitly different simulation routes, not two GPU engines.",
    "Public no-pixels timing uses one public action and still returns its final owned State, reward, observation and info; states=None suppresses history only.",
    "Public with-pixels timing adds the final frame. render_saved_state measures a fixed saved reset State. Rendering records backend=auto, not the resolved renderer implementation.",
    "Raw Warp measures two runtime.advance calls with precomputed controls, including interop and runtime guards. Raw native measures sequential local CPU lanes without public task/IPC/snapshot/render overhead. Raw is not a kernel-only comparison.",
    "Construction and first public step each have one timed sample. Reset and restore are separate stages. First-step memory profiling is an extra untimed second call, not a native/driver peak during cold capture.",
    "Construction measures the environment constructor and model initialization. Imports and initial CUDA context setup precede its timer; it does not measure total process startup.",
    "Each steady stage has five warmups and ten synchronized samples in this configuration. Physics advances during the step samples; this is one seed and zero normalized actions, not a workload distribution or tail-latency study.",
    "Fresh worker processes isolate records, but disk JIT caches can survive. First-step latency is not a guaranteed cold-compilation measurement.",
    "RSS and NVML are before/after samples, not transient peaks. RSS sums may count shared pages in multiple workers. NVML device totals include other processes. Stage allocations can include retained allocations from earlier phases.",
    "Torch allocator peaks exclude non-Torch Warp/driver allocations; tracemalloc excludes native allocations. Parent CPU/wall ratios omit child simulation workers and GPU utilization.",
    "The baseline revision is a caller label; native was measured from this worktree, not a separately checked-out baseline. Source hashes provide implementation provenance.",
    "For continued aggregates, each raw segment retains its own machine, device UUID and versions; ratios are allowed only within eligible same-segment native/Warp pairs.",
    "Performance evidence does not establish numerical correctness; numerical acceptance remains deferred."
  ],
